{
  "schema": 1,
  "readme": "Per-suite engine wall time in seconds, the weights RunTests.ps1 -Shards divides the catalog by. Regenerate from the shard reports of one warm full run (.scratch\\engine\\owner-<pid>\\shardNofM\\test-report.json): a serial run of the whole catalog measures one process's timings, not a shard's under its siblings' contention. These numbers are awareness for the balancer alone: a stale weight costs balance, never correctness, since every shard still reports its own verdicts and the merge checks the shards cover the selection exactly once.",
  "measuredFrom": "a warm complete gate run on the development machine for the suites the gate runs, and the last full-catalog run for the release tier's, all passing",
  "defaultSeconds": 1.5,
  "groupsReadme": "Suites that must share one shard because the second reads the first's worlds out of that process DecodeCache; splitting them costs about 3 s of decode each.",
  "groups": [
    ["mesh-light-blink", "mesh-light-fade"]
  ],
  "aloneReadme": "Suites that take a shard of their own. A TAA frame has Godot build the advanced variants of every shader alive in its process, about 25 MB each, so beside a shard's worlds the one suite that must draw a process's first TAA frame holds about 5 GB more than the shard needs (analysis/shard-memory/FINDINGS.md).",
  "alone": ["graphics-retext-compiles"],
